NAME
    tile - ASCII-decode one 8x8 tile from memory

SYNOPSIS
    tile <space> <addr> <bpp>

DESCRIPTION
    Decodes one 8x8 tile at hex <addr> in memory space <space> and prints
    its pixels as an 8x8 ASCII grid of hex palette indices (using '.' for
    color index 0). The meaning of <bpp> is core-specific (for example,
    2, 4, or 8 bits per pixel on SNES).

    Tile decoding is provided by the loaded core because pixel layouts are
    console-specific. Cores that do not expose tile decoding return no
    pixels, and 'tile' reports that and exits with status 1.

EXAMPLES
    tile VRAM 0 4
    tile VRAM 2000 2

EXIT STATUS
    0   Tile decoded and printed (or usage message printed).
    1   Core does not decode tiles, no target attached, unknown space,
        invalid hex argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    tilemap(1), pal(1), sprites(1), mem(1), spaces(1)
